; Generated by c64-source. Edit the values here: generate keeps them.
; The switches of the build. Each switch is 0 or 1: change a value, then build again.
; The defaults give the clean program: copy protection, trainers, cheats and
; changes of a crack are 0, and the fixes of the releases are 1.
; generate adds a new switch with its default and removes a switch that the
; knowledge does not have. The build of a release does not read this file.

; Changes of a crack: off by default
CRACK_MAYDAY = 0 ; on in MAYDAY. $2c3e-$2c3f, $2c88-$2c89, $39ba-$39bb, $39cd-$39ce. Mayday! (2023): the disk code takes the device number from $ba (FA) in place of the fixed drive 8, so that the release works with drives 8-11 (the note file READMENOTE of the release says so). The bytes without the change come from v2, a build of the same source: no v1 release has them.

; Start screen: on by default
START_SCREEN = 1 ; the loader shows the start screen and waits for a key or a fire button. 0 starts the program at once. Only the clean build has it: a release and LEFTOVERS = 1 have none

; Leftovers: off by default
LEFTOVERS = 0 ; 632 bytes in 17 files in leftovers/ that nothing uses. 1 builds them, so main.asm gives the bytes of the program. Each release has them. The loader never loads them
